Build command g++ main.cpp -o test -I./ -L./build -lscam  -lpthread

Run command LD_LIBRARY_PATH=./build ./test

Main functions
    Automatic device enumeration and format configuration
    Scan all USB cameras, get supported formats and auto-configure. Defaults to selecting the first format.
    The program extracts VID:PID when detecting devices. If the 5th digit of the PID is a/b/c, exposure start time is used as the time baseline; if d/e/f, exposure end time is used. 
Dynamic terminal display
    Continuously refresh and display detailed info for each frame on the current terminal, including:
	Logical device index, image format, resolution, data size, real-time FPS
	Exposure start/end time, exposure duration
	11 sets of IMU data associated with the device (Acceleration, Gyroscope, Timestamp)
Keyboard save
    Press the Space key to save the current frame shown on the screen. It automatically creates a subfolder named with the current system time (YYYYMMDD_HHMMSSZZZ), containing: 
	YYYYMMDD_HHMMSSZZZ.jpg - JPG image dumped from current frame
	YYYYMMDD_HHMMSSZZZ.txt - Text file containing frame metadata and detailed 11-set IMU data table

Hardware requirements
    At least 1 camera supporting the SCAM protocol. The program auto-selects the first detected available device and starts real-time display. 

The program continuously refreshes the terminal (clear and redraw) to show the latest frame information. Example: 
Camera 0: RGB24 1920x1080, size=6220800 bytes, fps=30.00
exposure: start=  1234567890 us end=  1234568890 us, duration=    1000 us
[g] 0x0 Acc=(  0.123456, -0.234567,  9.810000) Gyro=(  0.001234,  0.002345, -0.003456) time=  1234567900 us
[g] 0x1 Acc=(  0.123456, -0.234567,  9.810000) Gyro=(  0.001234,  0.002345, -0.003456) time=  1234567920 us
...

Camera X: Logical device index
Format, resolution, data size, real-time FPS
exposure: Exposure start time, Exposure end time, Exposure duration (microseconds)
IMU line: IMU sample index, Acceleration (X/Y/Z), Gyroscope (X/Y/Z), Timestamp
